### Why entropy is better here than maximum probability

I would also keep the implementation scientifically. Maximum softmax confidence considers essentially only the largest class probability, whereas entropy reflects the **entire predictive distribution**.

For example:

\[
[0.60,0.39,0.005,0.005]
\]

and

\[
[0.60,0.15,0.15,0.10]
\]

both have maximum probability \(0.60\), but their uncertainty structures are different. Entropy can capture that distinction.

So for your paper, the entropy-based version gives a more convincing interpretation of “prediction uncertainty.”

